   "format": "short_answer",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Consider the curve x^2 + 3y^2 - 2xy = 24, for which dy/dx = (x - y)/(x - 3y). For a positive constant k, the vertical line x = k is tangent to the curve. Find k."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 6
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "A vertical tangent needs the denominator to vanish: x - 3y = 0, so x = 3y.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            3,
            "y"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Substitute x = 3y into the curve: 9y^2 + 3y^2 - 6y^2 = 6y^2 = 24, so y = 2 or y = -2.",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At y = 2 the point is (6, 2), and the numerator there is 6 - 2 = 4, which is nonzero, so the tangent is vertical.",
         "mathjson": 4
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The positive value is k = 6.",
         "mathjson": 6
      }
   ],
